645
00:26:24.240 --> 00:26:25.800
And I was very excited about it.

646
00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:27.600
Bob Odenkirk was in it.

647
00:26:27.860 --> 00:26:29.420
Mark Maron was in it.

648
00:26:29.580 --> 00:26:30.960
It had a really kind of great caSt.

649
00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:33.540
And I was walking to the table read.

650
00:26:33.740 --> 00:26:35.640
Wait, wait, Rain, Rain, what was it called?

651
00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:36.740
Do you know the name of it?

652
00:26:37.040 --> 00:26:37.780
Oh, boy.

653
00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:38.860
It'll come to me.

654
00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:40.600
I can't remember right now.

655
00:26:40.700 --> 00:26:44.240
Oh, real life, still life, something like that.

656
00:26:44.560 --> 00:26:45.220
I'll look it up.

657
00:26:45.220 --> 00:26:46.460
Okay, go on, go on, go on.

658
00:26:46.580 --> 00:26:47.140
I can't remember.

659
00:26:48.860 --> 00:26:53.340
And I was on the way to the table read, which is something that actors you do at the studio

660
00:26:53.340 --> 00:26:54.220
or you used to do.

661
00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:58.760
You all sit in a room behind a table and you read it out loud and all the executives are

662
00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:03.620
