00:27:03.620 --> 00:27:05.080
read, give notes, et cetera.

664
00:27:05.740 --> 00:27:07.060
Very common occurrence.

665
00:27:07.300 --> 00:27:18.220
On my way there, I ran into this NBC executive that I knew at the time, who I had met a couple

666
00:27:18.220 --> 00:27:18.480
times.

667
00:27:18.620 --> 00:27:19.680
I forget why.

668
00:27:19.980 --> 00:27:21.320
And I was like, oh, hi.

669
00:27:21.460 --> 00:27:22.740
It was Vernon, Vernon Sanders.

670
00:27:22.900 --> 00:27:24.040
Oh, we love Vernon.

671
00:27:24.380 --> 00:27:24.840
Yes.

672
00:27:25.100 --> 00:27:25.660
Yeah, yeah.

673
00:27:25.840 --> 00:27:26.940
He's in Amazon now.

674
00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:28.320
And a nice guy.

675
00:27:28.320 --> 00:27:29.580
And I was like, hi, Vernon.

676
00:27:29.660 --> 00:27:30.260
And he's like, hi.

677
00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:31.520
He's like, what's going on?

678
00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:37.320
He goes, well, I'm so excited because we just landed the rights to the BBC office.

679
00:27:39.070 --> 00:27:41.690
I had seen a couple episodes.

680
00:27:41.930 --> 00:27:46.730
My friend Sam had them recorded from someone in England on a VHS.

681
00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:49.450
It was before they were like available in the United States.

682
00:27:49.610 --> 00:27:50.570
It was really early on.

683
00:27:51.010 --> 00:27:53.190
I had seen them and I just loved them.

684
00:27:53.330 --> 00:27:56.790
And I, and inside and outside, I was like, oh, that's great.

685
00:27:57.010 --> 00:27:57.270
That's great.

686
00:27:57.330 --> 00:27:57.670
Inside.

687
00:27:57.810 --> 00:27:59.290
I was like, oh, God damn it.

688
00:27:59.730 --> 00:28:00.850
I want to be in that show.

689
00:28:00.990 --> 00:28:03.030
That show, that show's so awesome.

690
00:28:04.990 --> 00:28:07.050
And so I was like, okay, see you later.

691
00:28:07.310 --> 00:28:08.190
Went to the table read.

692
00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:11.210
This is one of the most incredible experiences.

693
00:28:11.430 --> 00:28:14.270
In fact, Kent Zvornak was the producer on it.

694
00:28:14.430 --> 00:28:15.510
Oh my gosh.

695
00:28:15.670 --> 00:28:15.850
Wow.

696
00:28:16.050 --> 00:28:16.450
Kentopedia?

697
00:28:16.930 --> 00:28:17.250
Yeah.

698
00:28:17.630 --> 00:28:20.530
So we did the table read and this was an infamous event.

699
00:28:20.770 --> 00:28:21.590
We did the table read.

700
00:28:21.690 --> 00:28:26.510
It went so bad that it, the, the plug was pulled immediately.

701
00:28:26.510 --> 00:28:27.890
They canceled it.

702
00:28:27.970 --> 00:28:29.170
They didn't, you didn't even shoot it.

