00:28:30.950 --> 00:28:31.970
They had sets built.

705
00:28:32.170 --> 00:28:33.490
We had plane tickets.

706
00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:35.590
We had hotel rooms booked.

707
00:28:35.890 --> 00:28:40.110
We, I was supposed to fly the next morning and then start shooting in like two days.

708
00:28:40.450 --> 00:28:42.390
And the table read went so poorly.

709
00:28:42.390 --> 00:28:46.210
We found the name, by the way, the name is Slice O' Life.

710
00:28:46.890 --> 00:28:47.950
Slice O' Life.

711
00:28:48.170 --> 00:28:50.410
That's what, I knew it had life in it and an S.

712
00:28:52.410 --> 00:28:54.790
But so all of a sudden I was free to do the office.

713
00:28:54.790 --> 00:28:56.190
So I called my agents.

714
00:28:56.190 --> 00:28:58.050
I was like, I'd really like to audition for this office.

715
00:28:58.290 --> 00:29:03.250
And yes, I was, I was the first person to audition on the very first day.

716
00:29:03.410 --> 00:29:07.570
Alison Jones, the casting director kind of knew me from six feet under and some other things.

717
00:29:07.570 --> 00:29:13.770
I was so excited and I auditioned for both Dwight and Michael on that first day.

718
00:29:14.250 --> 00:29:18.310
And she keeps threatening to release my Michael Scott audition.

719
00:29:18.590 --> 00:29:23.410
It is truly terrible because I just did a Ricky Gervais impersonation.

720
00:29:23.570 --> 00:29:25.410
I didn't know what else to do.

721
00:29:25.590 --> 00:29:28.110
So I was kind of pulling on my tie a lot.

722
00:29:28.250 --> 00:29:33.870
And, um, it was, but Dwight, I knew I was like, this is completely in my wheelhouse.

723
00:29:33.870 --> 00:29:36.850
I know exactly who this person is.

724
00:29:37.070 --> 00:29:38.770
This guy is in my DNA.

725
00:29:39.010 --> 00:29:43.610
I have cousins who are really not that different from Dwight Schrute.

726
00:29:44.030 --> 00:29:46.370
And, um, the rest is history.

727
00:29:47.210 --> 00:29:51.550
Well, Rain, I remember being paired with you during the screen tests.

728
00:29:52.050 --> 00:29:52.570
Yeah.

729
00:29:52.790 --> 00:29:54.910
And they were mixing and matching us.

730
00:29:55.290 --> 00:29:59.510
There were like four Pams and four Jims and four Dwights and a few Michaels.

731
00:29:59.750 --> 00:30:03.850
Bob Odenkirk was one of the Michaels, which is so crazy because I guess he was,

732
00:30:03.850 --> 00:30:08.590
he was available as well since Slice O' Life didn't go forward.

733
00:30:09.150 --> 00:30:10.590
And Ken's Murnack was available.

734
00:30:10.950 --> 00:30:11.190
Yeah.

735
00:30:11.430 --> 00:30:11.630
Wow.

736
00:30:11.730 --> 00:30:14.410
We really, we got a lot of folks from Slice O' Life.

737
00:30:14.590 --> 00:30:15.410
We got lucky there.

738
00:30:15.570 --> 00:30:16.250
We scored.

739
00:30:16.690 --> 00:30:23.130
But Rain, I remember being paired with you and I, I mean, I couldn't believe it.

740
00:30:23.330 --> 00:30:30.390
Of all of us, of all of us, you were 100% there from the beginning.

741
00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:36.070
I feel like from that moment that I did that first audition scene with you, everybody else,

742
00:30:36.590 --> 00:30:39.930
I was paired, like I was paired with John and I was like, oh yeah, this is great.

743
00:30:40.110 --> 00:30:41.950
And, and Steve and everybody.

744
00:30:42.110 --> 00:30:49.210
But Rain, you were just like, I didn't even know where Rain began and Dwight ended or Dwight

745
00:30:49.210 --> 00:30:50.330
began and Rain ended.

746
00:30:50.330 --> 00:30:51.610
I mean, it was so fluid.

747
00:30:51.950 --> 00:30:53.010
It was amazing.

748
00:30:53.710 --> 00:30:57.130
But you were, I have to say there's a mutual admiration society.

749
00:30:57.610 --> 00:31:01.610
For those who don't know, Jenna was totally in Pam, dressed as Pam.

750
00:31:01.930 --> 00:31:08.010
You were reading the book on John Belushi, Wired, that you thought Pam would be reading.

751
00:31:08.250 --> 00:31:10.390
It was in the script that she was reading it.

752
00:31:10.450 --> 00:31:11.710
So I read the whole novel.

753
00:31:12.010 --> 00:31:13.250
I read the whole thing.

754
00:31:13.430 --> 00:31:15.390
I was like, my character read it.

755
00:31:15.390 --> 00:31:16.110
I'll read it.

756
00:31:17.190 --> 00:31:17.630
Yeah.

757
00:31:18.130 --> 00:31:21.390
And, um, but you were Pam in the waiting room too.

758
00:31:21.670 --> 00:31:24.410
I, um, but that was so much fun.

759
00:31:24.550 --> 00:31:30.510
And we had, I don't know if they'd ever released that audition, but that improvisation where

760
00:31:30.510 --> 00:31:34.870
I was just sitting, I was kneeling like way too close to you.

761
00:31:35.030 --> 00:31:35.290
Yeah.

762
00:31:35.410 --> 00:31:39.090
Like, which is something I love to do as Dwight is like, he doesn't have an understanding

