Hold the mic, please.

1292
00:59:55.120 --> 00:59:55.720
Hi, Kevin.

1293
00:59:56.600 --> 00:59:57.220
Hey, Lynn.

1294
00:59:58.200 --> 00:59:59.380
Did you get my message?

1295
01:00:00.340 --> 01:00:01.620
Um, yeah.

1296
01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:03.940
I've been really busy.

1297
01:00:05.140 --> 01:00:05.700
Oh.

1298
01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:07.620
It's okay.

1299
01:00:08.500 --> 01:00:12.380
Yeah, I'm probably going to be busy for the next 20 days or so.

1300
01:00:15.520 --> 01:00:16.960
So, yeah.

1301
01:00:18.660 --> 01:00:19.080
Bye.

1302
01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:24.440
You're going to be busy for the next 20 days or so.

1303
01:00:24.720 --> 01:00:25.980
I thought you liked Lynn.

1304
01:00:26.120 --> 01:00:26.940
I do like Lynn.

1305
01:00:27.460 --> 01:00:29.240
That's what Andy told me to say.

1306
01:00:30.400 --> 01:00:31.360
Uh-huh.

1307
01:00:32.220 --> 01:00:32.680
Right?

1308
01:00:33.460 --> 01:00:39.140
So, Jim and Pam are learning that Andy has been giving Kevin some pretty bad advice.

1309
01:00:39.400 --> 01:00:39.740
Yeah.

1310
01:00:39.960 --> 01:00:45.800
He likes Lynn but tells her, you know, he didn't return her messages and he's going to be busy for 20 days.

1311
01:00:46.420 --> 01:00:46.940
Wow.

1312
01:00:47.900 --> 01:00:48.840
That's amazing.

1313
01:00:49.260 --> 01:00:51.840
Jim and Pam can't let Andy do this to Kevin.

1314
01:00:51.980 --> 01:00:53.420
So, they start giving him advice, right?

1315
01:00:53.540 --> 01:00:54.620
Just ask her out.

1316
01:00:54.620 --> 01:01:01.460
And in the deleted scenes, you really get a sneak peek into where Andy's brain is at.

1317
01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:03.000
You got to hear this talking head.

1318
01:01:03.340 --> 01:01:05.720
I was raised to be a gentleman around women.

1319
01:01:05.880 --> 01:01:08.900
But when your fiancé is Satan, that doesn't work.

1320
01:01:09.240 --> 01:01:13.660
So, I have some new ideas and new techniques and I'm trying them out.

1321
01:01:14.140 --> 01:01:15.640
Kevin Malone is my guinea pig.

1322
01:01:16.580 --> 01:01:17.480
Aw, man.

1323
01:01:17.480 --> 01:01:18.840
I wish that had stayed in.

1324
01:01:19.020 --> 01:01:20.340
Doesn't that explain it all?

1325
01:01:20.340 --> 01:01:21.360
Well, it does.

1326
01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:30.020
I mean, I think I was able to realize that the reason that Andy is being this way is because he's still reeling from his breakup with Angela.

1327
01:01:30.240 --> 01:01:33.280
But that really would have been great.

1328
01:01:33.480 --> 01:01:34.100
I know.

1329
01:01:34.100 --> 01:01:37.160
Because, I mean, I don't think Andy's a bad guy.

1330
01:01:37.160 --> 01:01:40.700
But he's clearly hurt and acting out and using poor Kevin.

1331
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:41.960
Well, listen.

1332
01:01:42.440 --> 01:01:44.220
Jim's going to get a phone call now.

1333
01:01:44.760 --> 01:01:45.600
Guess what?

1334
01:01:45.860 --> 01:01:46.200
What?

1335
01:01:46.460 --> 01:01:49.380
His client, Tom, has found a golden ticket.

1336
01:01:49.380 --> 01:01:52.220
Tom from Blue Cross of Pennsylvania.

1337
01:01:52.620 --> 01:01:53.580
Our biggest client.

1338
01:01:54.140 --> 01:01:54.680
Uh-oh.

1339
01:01:55.140 --> 01:01:57.540
Oscar, how much is that going to cost us?

1340
01:01:57.540 --> 01:01:58.800
Michael wants to know.

1341
01:01:58.980 --> 01:02:00.020
It's going to hurt a bit.

1342
01:02:00.520 --> 01:02:02.200
Well, what about this?

1343
01:02:02.680 --> 01:02:06.100
Guys, Tom found all five golden tickets.

1344
01:02:06.740 --> 01:02:07.900
Holy moly.

1345
01:02:08.220 --> 01:02:10.380
Did they say one per customer?

1346
01:02:10.920 --> 01:02:11.180
Nope.

1347
01:02:11.260 --> 01:02:11.540
Nope.

1348
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:17.420
Our biggest client just got 50% off their total order with us.

1349
01:02:17.580 --> 01:02:19.060
I mean, this is a huge win.

1350
01:02:19.380 --> 01:02:20.880
Talk about winning the golden ticket.

1351
01:02:21.100 --> 01:02:22.640
He won all the golden tickets.

1352
01:02:22.660 --> 01:02:23.680
He won all of them.

1353
01:02:24.120 --> 01:02:29.220
This made me think, Jenna, have you ever won like a really big ticket item?

1354
01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:31.040
I don't think so.

1355
01:02:31.400 --> 01:02:36.480
I called my mom because I know my Aunt Anne has won things.

1356
01:02:36.660 --> 01:02:38.980
Like, she signs up for, you know, raffles and things.

1357
01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:40.200
And she's won trips.

1358
01:02:40.560 --> 01:02:41.000
Really?

1359
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:42.380
Yeah, she's super lucky.

1360
01:02:42.680 --> 01:02:45.120
And I was like, Mom, doesn't Aunt Anne win a lot of things?

1361
01:02:45.180 --> 01:02:48.520
And she said, well, you know, your dad won a very big ticket item.

1362
01:02:49.300 --> 01:02:50.700
What did your dad win?

1363
01:02:50.860 --> 01:02:52.720
And I was like, Mom, what are you talking about?

1364
01:02:52.800 --> 01:02:54.780
And she said, well, this was before you were born.

1365
01:02:55.340 --> 01:02:57.740
And Jenna, this story just delighted me so much.

1366
01:02:57.840 --> 01:03:00.420
One, because, you know, my dad's passed away.

1367
01:03:00.520 --> 01:03:03.620
And so any new information, because, you know, you play every memory.

1368
01:03:03.760 --> 01:03:04.420
You look at everything.

1369
01:03:04.560 --> 01:03:09.240
But anything that you hear about someone you loved who's no longer with you, you just,

1370
01:03:09.460 --> 01:03:12.140
oh, it's like this beautiful, wonderful thing.

1371
01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:18.760
So my mom said, oh, yeah, before you were born, we had just moved to Lafayette, Louisiana.

1372
01:03:19.760 --> 01:03:22.240
And the school was having a fundraiser.

1373
01:03:22.400 --> 01:03:27.540
And they were raffling off a brand new pink station wagon.

1374
01:03:27.860 --> 01:03:28.200
What?

1375
01:03:28.960 --> 01:03:31.160
She said it had a cream white top.

1376
01:03:31.400 --> 01:03:35.360
And your dad went and donated some money and signed up.

1377
01:03:35.620 --> 01:03:37.360
And he won the car.

1378
01:03:37.660 --> 01:03:39.920
Your dad won a pink station wagon?

1379
01:03:39.920 --> 01:03:42.260
Yes, and she said, and it was a very good car.

1380
01:03:42.260 --> 01:03:43.860
And we drove it for a long time.

1381
01:03:44.920 --> 01:03:47.540
Do any of your sisters remember this car?

1382
01:03:47.740 --> 01:03:50.360
I was like, my sister, Billie, said she remembers it.

1383
01:03:50.440 --> 01:03:51.560
But I was like, oh, my goodness.

1384
01:03:51.680 --> 01:03:53.760
And my mom's like, I know we have a picture somewhere.

1385
01:03:53.960 --> 01:03:55.220
I said, Mom, please.

1386
01:03:55.580 --> 01:03:56.620
And I have to see it.

1387
01:03:56.700 --> 01:04:01.000
And she said, oh, Ange, your dad was so tickled that he won that car.

1388
01:04:01.200 --> 01:04:02.620
He was so excited.

1389
01:04:03.860 --> 01:04:07.820
And she said, and it was a light pink with a cream top.

1390
01:04:07.820 --> 01:04:10.100
And they drove it around for years.

1391
01:04:11.040 --> 01:04:12.800
I love that story.

1392
01:04:12.800 --> 01:04:13.420
I know.

1393
01:04:13.720 --> 01:04:14.760
It made my day.

1394
01:04:15.060 --> 01:04:22.540
You know, I have been pitching for years a documentary series that I call Little Winners.

1395
01:04:23.060 --> 01:04:30.700
And it is all about people who have won, not the lottery, but raffles.

1396
01:04:31.800 --> 01:04:38.380
And they get something like this car or like a new recliner or like a trip, right?

1397
01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:41.120
And how did it affect their life?

1398
01:04:41.800 --> 01:04:42.740
Little Winners.

1399
01:04:42.940 --> 01:04:44.140
No one will buy it from me.

1400
01:04:44.240 --> 01:04:45.340
No one wants to make it.

1401
01:04:45.420 --> 01:04:46.500
I pitch it all the time.

1402
01:04:46.720 --> 01:04:48.260
I will no one make Little Winners.

1403
01:04:48.260 --> 01:04:49.920
I love Little Winners.

1404
01:04:50.160 --> 01:04:52.540
We could do it as a podcast and have the winner on.

1405
01:04:52.660 --> 01:04:54.040
And they could tell us all about it.

1406
01:04:54.500 --> 01:04:55.320
Here's the thing.

1407
01:04:55.560 --> 01:04:58.340
You know, I like to think about my parents.

1408
01:04:58.460 --> 01:04:59.260
They were young parents.

1409
01:04:59.420 --> 01:05:03.100
They had three young girls at this time and what that car meant to them.

1410
01:05:03.220 --> 01:05:06.940
And then I also think about the car dealer there in Lafayette, Louisiana,

1411
01:05:06.940 --> 01:05:11.980
and how the school, probably the superintendent, was buddies with the guy at the dealership

1412
01:05:11.980 --> 01:05:14.220
and was like, what do you got that we can raffle off?

1413
01:05:14.220 --> 01:05:18.620
And he's like, well, that pink station wagon, no one wants it.

1414
01:05:18.880 --> 01:05:20.080
We can't sell it.

1415
01:05:20.080 --> 01:05:21.100
It's a write-off.

1416
01:05:21.260 --> 01:05:22.420
I'll give it to you.

1417
01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:25.920
Okay.

1418
01:05:26.220 --> 01:05:26.560
Amazing.

1419
01:05:26.860 --> 01:05:27.220
Amazing.

1420
01:05:27.480 --> 01:05:32.880
So Michael is spiraling out, though, because he's realizing Blue Cross from Pennsylvania

1421
01:05:32.880 --> 01:05:34.420
getting this many golden tickets.

1422
01:05:34.680 --> 01:05:35.980
He's going to get fired.

1423
01:05:36.280 --> 01:05:39.560
And Jim is upset, too, because that's his commission.

1424
01:05:39.840 --> 01:05:40.400
Oh, right.

1425
01:05:40.600 --> 01:05:40.840
Right?

1426
01:05:40.840 --> 01:05:44.060
So Michael is going to storm down to the warehouse.

1427
01:05:44.240 --> 01:05:45.940
I love the beginning of this scene.

1428
01:05:45.940 --> 01:05:47.260
This scene is brilliant.

1429
01:05:47.500 --> 01:05:52.220
He goes barreling in going, hey, hey, hey, you idiot, to Daryl.

1430
01:05:52.360 --> 01:05:54.660
And Daryl says, start over.

1431
01:05:55.140 --> 01:05:55.980
So good.

1432
01:05:56.180 --> 01:05:57.640
I was like, I'm keeping that.

1433
01:05:57.780 --> 01:05:58.740
I am keeping that.

1434
01:05:58.820 --> 01:06:02.140
The next time one of the kids has a moment where they're sassing me, I'm going to be like,

1435
01:06:02.680 --> 01:06:03.340
start over.

1436
01:06:03.920 --> 01:06:04.360
Exactly.

1437
01:06:04.360 --> 01:06:06.720
And then Michael comes back with, sir?

1438
01:06:08.520 --> 01:06:09.920
That was all in the script.

1439
01:06:09.920 --> 01:06:10.920
I looked that up.

1440
01:06:10.920 --> 01:06:11.680
I had to know.

1441
01:06:11.740 --> 01:06:12.320
So did I.

1442
01:06:12.900 --> 01:06:14.840
Michael's like, Daryl, how could this happen?

1443
01:06:15.000 --> 01:06:15.840
How could this happen?

1444
01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:20.020
And he says, I put three pallets on the truck for Blue Cross every week.

1445
01:06:20.740 --> 01:06:22.040
Where were you putting the boxes?

1446
01:06:22.040 --> 01:06:23.020
Were they near each other?

1447
01:06:23.320 --> 01:06:26.100
And Michael's like, I need to ask you something.

1448
01:06:26.160 --> 01:06:27.300
I need you to be honest with me.

1449
01:06:28.180 --> 01:06:29.260
What is a pallet?

1450
01:06:30.960 --> 01:06:31.920
So good.

1451
01:06:33.040 --> 01:06:33.920
So good.

1452
01:06:34.720 --> 01:06:36.260
David Wallace is not happy.

1453
01:06:36.880 --> 01:06:37.840
He calls.

1454
01:06:38.120 --> 01:06:39.340
Pam takes the call.

1455
01:06:39.700 --> 01:06:42.360
But Michael is sort of sneaking out of his office.

1456
01:06:42.500 --> 01:06:44.340
He's taken off his Willy Wonka outfit.

1457
01:06:44.640 --> 01:06:46.160
Yeah, he's getting rid of the evidence.

1458
01:06:46.340 --> 01:06:46.660
Yes.

1459
01:06:46.780 --> 01:06:48.200
He's like, I am not here.

1460
01:06:48.300 --> 01:06:48.960
I am not here.

1461
01:06:49.120 --> 01:06:53.460
So Pam has to say that he's at a civil rights rally at the Lincoln Memorial.

1462
01:06:53.740 --> 01:06:55.920
Which I want to point out is in Washington.

1463
01:06:56.240 --> 01:06:56.540
Yeah.

1464
01:06:56.960 --> 01:06:59.120
He's gone to Washington, D.C.

1465
01:06:59.260 --> 01:06:59.720
I guess.

1466
01:06:59.900 --> 01:07:04.000
In the same day, he's going to go to a civil rights movement in Washington, D.C.

1467
01:07:04.120 --> 01:07:05.980
and get a colonoscopy in Scranton.

1468
01:07:06.700 --> 01:07:07.260
Exactly.

1469
01:07:08.920 --> 01:07:12.860
Well, Michael tosses his Willy Wonka costume into a dumpster.

1470
01:07:13.040 --> 01:07:16.160
He's now wearing a Pioneer's football shirt.

1471
01:07:16.820 --> 01:07:18.980
And I had to look this up.

1472
01:07:19.200 --> 01:07:25.200
This is a minor league football team from Wilkes-Barre Scranton that played in the AF2.

1473
01:07:25.200 --> 01:07:30.800
And they had a really strong season in 2009 when we shot this episode.

1474
01:07:31.180 --> 01:07:36.280
It's kind of like perfect that he's wearing this shirt because they only ended up losing

1475
01:07:36.280 --> 01:07:38.000
two of their games that year.

1476
01:07:38.140 --> 01:07:39.560
They made it to the playoffs.

1477
01:07:39.560 --> 01:07:45.520
Then they made it all the way to the Arena Cup, which is like the Super Bowl of AF2 football.

1478
01:07:45.520 --> 01:07:50.200
They ended up losing, but it was like a great, great season for them.

1479
01:07:50.280 --> 01:07:51.220
They were kind of on a roll.

1480
01:07:51.360 --> 01:07:53.120
Their previous season had been good as well.

1481
01:07:53.360 --> 01:07:54.340
I love it.

1482
01:07:54.500 --> 01:07:56.500
I love every time we have-

1483
01:07:56.500 --> 01:07:57.380
Every single time.

1484
01:07:57.500 --> 01:08:02.100
...these local references on the show in ways that don't even get mentioned.

1485
01:08:02.360 --> 01:08:02.560
Right.

1486
01:08:02.560 --> 01:08:08.560
We never even mentioned this shirt, but there it is, just creating specificity.

1487
01:08:08.700 --> 01:08:09.300
I love it.

1488
01:08:09.820 --> 01:08:12.460
Michael's going to make an announcement, everyone to the conference room.

1489
01:08:12.600 --> 01:08:14.320
He's- a lot of announcements in this episode.

1490
01:08:14.420 --> 01:08:14.500
Yeah.

1491
01:08:14.500 --> 01:08:15.180
A lot of announcements.

1492
01:08:15.900 --> 01:08:19.840
He's really, I think, just trying to find a way out.

1493
01:08:20.040 --> 01:08:25.380
He says he has a big net where he takes all of their subconscious ideas and tries to turn

1494
01:08:25.380 --> 01:08:26.140
them into something.

1495
01:08:26.640 --> 01:08:29.380
And Michael's like, guys, guys, they're not going to fire us.

1496
01:08:29.520 --> 01:08:29.980
We're fine.

1497
01:08:29.980 --> 01:08:32.960
And Oscar's like, what do you call shutting down a branch?

1498
01:08:33.600 --> 01:08:38.900
And then Michael says, someone needs to come up with a golden ticket idea to get them out

1499
01:08:38.900 --> 01:08:39.480
of this mess.

1500
01:08:39.900 --> 01:08:40.400
Mm-hmm.

1501
01:08:40.840 --> 01:08:41.280
You know?

1502
01:08:41.800 --> 01:08:45.580
And Pam says, do you mean an idea that blows up in our faces later?

1503
01:08:45.960 --> 01:08:46.320
Oh.

1504
01:08:46.400 --> 01:08:47.200
That kind of idea?

1505
01:08:47.240 --> 01:08:48.280
That's some Pam sass.

1506
01:08:48.440 --> 01:08:49.740
That is some Pam sass.

1507
01:08:50.480 --> 01:08:53.840
So while Michael's up at the top of the conference room, he's wearing a suit jacket.

1508
01:08:54.080 --> 01:08:54.340
Mm-hmm.

1509
01:08:54.340 --> 01:08:55.840
And I'm thinking, where did that come from?

1510
01:08:55.840 --> 01:08:59.600
Because the last time we saw him, he was at the dumpster in his Pioneer's football shirt.

1511
01:08:59.600 --> 01:08:59.960
Right.

1512
01:09:00.380 --> 01:09:01.260
I looked it up.

1513
01:09:02.120 --> 01:09:03.320
It's Andy's jacket.

1514
01:09:03.580 --> 01:09:04.940
He's wearing Andy's jacket.

1515
01:09:04.940 --> 01:09:09.760
And there was a bit at the top of this scene that got cut where, as they're entering the

1516
01:09:09.760 --> 01:09:11.880
room, Michael says, Andy, give me your jacket.

1517
01:09:12.040 --> 01:09:13.220
You can do something for me.

1518
01:09:13.520 --> 01:09:14.560
I want your jacket.

1519
01:09:14.760 --> 01:09:19.400
So that is why he's now wearing this odd jacket over his football shirt.

1520
01:09:19.440 --> 01:09:21.200
Well, he's got to still look like the boss.

1521
01:09:21.200 --> 01:09:23.000
The phone's going to ring now.

1522
01:09:23.240 --> 01:09:23.860
Not good.

1523
01:09:24.000 --> 01:09:24.840
It's David Wallace.

1524
01:09:25.560 --> 01:09:28.060
Pam says Michael's having a colonoscopy.

1525
01:09:28.800 --> 01:09:32.220
I'm not sure that David Wallace believes it.

1526
01:09:32.640 --> 01:09:33.440
You think?

1527
01:09:34.600 --> 01:09:36.780
Because he was just in Washington.

1528
01:09:38.120 --> 01:09:43.460
Michael gets on the phone with him and literally is reading off the procedure of how you give

1529
01:09:43.460 --> 01:09:45.420
a colonoscopy off his computer.

1530
01:09:45.940 --> 01:09:47.240
It's pretty amazing.

1531
01:09:47.740 --> 01:09:49.400
But now it is clear.

1532
01:09:49.680 --> 01:09:53.580
David Wallace says, the company is going to lose a lot of money.

1533
01:09:53.940 --> 01:09:55.720
How did you let this happen?

1534
01:09:55.940 --> 01:09:57.500
Whose idea was it?

1535
01:09:57.720 --> 01:10:00.540
Someone's got to pay for this terrible idea.

1536
01:10:01.440 --> 01:10:04.100
Michael tells David Wallace it was Dwight.

1537
01:10:04.380 --> 01:10:05.780
Just so devious.

1538
01:10:06.180 --> 01:10:06.720
I know.

1539
01:10:07.040 --> 01:10:08.180
Oh, Michael.

1540
01:10:08.180 --> 01:10:12.860
It's like David Wallace is just naming people and he says, was it Dwight?

1541
01:10:13.200 --> 01:10:16.060
And Michael's like, yes.

1542
01:10:17.280 --> 01:10:20.620
Well, now Michael has got to convince Dwight to take the fall for him.

1543
01:10:21.760 --> 01:10:26.460
And so he's going to get out his diary and he's going to say, Dwight, I wrote it down

1544
01:10:26.460 --> 01:10:27.220
that it was your idea.

1545
01:10:27.380 --> 01:10:31.540
He tries to convince Dwight that Dwight is remembering wrong.

1546
01:10:31.920 --> 01:10:33.900
What happened this morning?

1547
01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:37.060
Now, you know, Dwight runs to get his diary.

1548
01:10:37.060 --> 01:10:40.040
It's like the dueling diaries where they're going back and forth.

1549
01:10:40.640 --> 01:10:43.980
Michael realizes he's not making any headway with this whole diary business.

1550
01:10:44.180 --> 01:10:46.860
So he says, would you like to go out to lunch with me?

1551
01:10:47.120 --> 01:10:47.920
Just the two of us.

1552
01:10:48.620 --> 01:10:51.360
And Dwight says, with all my heart.

1553
01:10:51.880 --> 01:10:54.180
This scene continues in the script, Jenna.

1554
01:10:54.460 --> 01:10:58.760
So after Dwight says, with all my heart, he says, but I already ate lunch.

1555
01:10:59.360 --> 01:11:01.940
And Michael says, it's 11 a.m.

1556
01:11:02.360 --> 01:11:05.220
Dwight says, as a farmer, I eat breakfast at 4.30.

1557
01:11:05.640 --> 01:11:07.840
At 10, I'm famished for lunch.

1558
01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:10.020
If you wait three hours, we can have supper.

1559
01:11:10.260 --> 01:11:10.460
Maybe.

1560
01:11:11.080 --> 01:11:12.120
Michael says, no, no, no.

1561
01:11:12.300 --> 01:11:14.540
How about we do something else you like?

1562
01:11:15.300 --> 01:11:17.760
Jenna, did you notice there are no scenes of them at the restaurant?

1563
01:11:18.660 --> 01:11:20.540
They're supposedly going to have lunch, right?

1564
01:11:20.660 --> 01:11:23.240
Because in the episode, Michael says, go have lunch.

1565
01:11:23.360 --> 01:11:25.260
We don't know that Dwight's already eaten.

1566
01:11:25.440 --> 01:11:27.040
All of that's been cut out, right?

1567
01:11:27.260 --> 01:11:30.960
And then the remainder of their scenes, they're on the side of the road.

1568
01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:32.020
They're taking a walk.

1569
01:11:32.020 --> 01:11:37.300
Well, here is a scene that was in the deleted scenes that I just love so much.

1570
01:11:37.520 --> 01:11:40.980
Of all the things that Dwight would want to do, guess what he loves to do?

1571
01:11:41.120 --> 01:11:42.220
Go for walks?

1572
01:11:42.820 --> 01:11:43.920
Oh, lady, no.

1573
01:11:44.800 --> 01:11:46.140
He likes a stroll.

1574
01:11:46.620 --> 01:11:49.380
Are you still taking those strolls that you like to take?

1575
01:11:49.600 --> 01:11:50.240
Thrice weekly.

1576
01:11:50.920 --> 01:11:53.200
Okay, let's go take a stroll together.

1577
01:11:53.500 --> 01:11:54.740
I thought you said my strolls were silly.

1578
01:11:54.840 --> 01:11:57.220
No, just because you can't call them walks.

1579
01:11:57.460 --> 01:11:58.220
You really want a stroll?

1580
01:11:59.200 --> 01:11:59.640
Yes.

1581
01:11:59.640 --> 01:12:01.720
Do you want a power stroll or just a regular stroll?

1582
01:12:02.400 --> 01:12:03.380
You call it.

1583
01:12:03.540 --> 01:12:04.200
Power stroll.

1584
01:12:05.460 --> 01:12:06.000
Okay.

1585
01:12:06.400 --> 01:12:07.140
Are you wearing sunblock?

1586
01:12:07.400 --> 01:12:07.840
Yes.

1587
01:12:07.960 --> 01:12:08.480
What SPF?

1588
01:12:08.740 --> 01:12:09.140
One.

1589
01:12:09.840 --> 01:12:10.960
That's like water.

1590
01:12:11.480 --> 01:12:12.600
I'll grab my tube.

1591
01:12:12.760 --> 01:12:13.080
Okay.

1592
01:12:13.820 --> 01:12:14.200
Oh.

1593
01:12:16.320 --> 01:12:17.820
He loves a stroll.

1594
01:12:18.120 --> 01:12:22.640
Clearly, it's like a whole thing with him and Michael about calling it a stroll or a walk.

1595
01:12:22.640 --> 01:12:33.080
Then there's another scene where they're down in the lobby and Hank is there and Dwight is putting sunscreen on Michael's face and Hank looks up and deadpan says,

1596
01:12:33.240 --> 01:12:34.960
you found somebody to go on a stroll.

1597
01:12:36.280 --> 01:12:37.920
And Dwight goes, I did.

1598
01:12:38.100 --> 01:12:39.600
And Hank goes, nice.

1599
01:12:40.140 --> 01:12:49.760
This is amazing because we got a ton of mail because people were pointing out Dwight's shoes in the scene when he is walking, a.k.a.

1600
01:12:49.940 --> 01:12:50.920
strolling with Michael.

1601
01:12:50.920 --> 01:12:58.520
Tons of people said, why does Dwight have on very white, very non-Dwight trainers?

1602
01:12:59.060 --> 01:13:01.160
Like, where did these come from?

1603
01:13:02.080 --> 01:13:06.820
And I looked in the script and it says, Michael and Dwight are walking.

1604
01:13:07.200 --> 01:13:12.860
Dwight is wearing sneakers and walks with his hands clasped behind his back.

1605
01:13:13.420 --> 01:13:19.160
That was like a script note, but I'm sure it was all based on this backstory that Dwight strolls three times a week.

1606
01:13:19.160 --> 01:13:20.040
He's got his sunblock.

1607
01:13:20.160 --> 01:13:21.020
He's got his shoes.

1608
01:13:21.220 --> 01:13:23.240
He probably has a little bag he takes to work.

1609
01:13:23.620 --> 01:13:28.160
Clearly, Hank knows how much Dwight loves a stroll and how he's been looking for a stroll buddy.

1610
01:13:28.400 --> 01:13:29.340
I love it.

1611
01:13:30.560 --> 01:13:31.520
I love it.

1612
01:13:31.540 --> 01:13:31.760
I know.

1613
01:13:31.880 --> 01:13:32.440
It tickled me.

1614
01:13:32.920 --> 01:13:35.520
Well, this stroll is not going to convince Dwight.

1615
01:13:35.880 --> 01:13:38.340
Dwight says, I am not going to fall on my sword for you.

1616
01:13:38.420 --> 01:13:39.360
It's not going to happen.

1617
01:13:39.720 --> 01:13:40.800
He's done it before.

1618
01:13:41.060 --> 01:13:42.940
He's fallen on his sword and it wasn't pleasant.

1619
01:13:42.980 --> 01:13:43.780
It wasn't.

1620
01:13:44.040 --> 01:13:45.980
Michael makes a pretty big speech to Dwight.

1621
01:13:46.080 --> 01:13:48.180
He's like, listen, why would you want to stay here?

1622
01:13:48.320 --> 01:13:48.580
Yeah.

1623
01:13:48.840 --> 01:13:49.660
You're cooped up.

1624
01:13:49.740 --> 01:13:51.720
You're not even dating Angela anymore.

1625
01:13:51.920 --> 01:13:52.980
You have a whole farm.

1626
01:13:53.240 --> 01:13:53.640
Yeah.

1627
01:13:54.280 --> 01:13:58.400
And he says, you know, on the other hand, I would be lost without Dunder Mifflin.

1628
01:13:58.400 --> 01:14:01.560
And Dwight says, what about Shulala, Michael?

1629
01:14:03.790 --> 01:14:06.530
This is a Mindy Kaling thing, for sure.

1630
01:14:06.770 --> 01:14:09.010
This has Mindy Kaling written all over it.

1631
01:14:09.150 --> 01:14:13.530
And then Michael has a talking head where he says, I have an idea for a fancy men's shoe

1632
01:14:13.530 --> 01:14:14.610
store called Shulala.

1633
01:14:14.870 --> 01:14:19.550
And it's just men's shoes for the special occasions in a man's life, like the day that

1634
01:14:19.550 --> 01:14:24.310
you get married or the day your wife has a baby or just for lounging around the house.

1635
01:14:24.530 --> 01:14:24.810
Yeah.

1636
01:14:24.990 --> 01:14:30.930
Well, we got some mail from Kayla G who said, I just want to let you ladies know that Michael

1637
01:14:30.930 --> 01:14:35.170
seems to have gotten Shulala up and running in Nelson, British Columbia.

1638
01:14:35.570 --> 01:14:36.090
Oh.

1639
01:14:36.090 --> 01:14:39.370
And I looked it up and sure enough, there is a Shulala.

1640
01:14:40.010 --> 01:14:45.570
According to their website, they are a boutique shoe store offering exquisite leather footwear

1641
01:14:45.570 --> 01:14:47.950
and handbags from all over the world.

1642
01:14:48.190 --> 01:14:52.530
They are a family run business that has been around since 1983.

1643
01:14:53.430 --> 01:14:53.790
Hmm.

1644
01:14:53.790 --> 01:14:59.050
Well, I want you guys to know that there is a Shulala in Lafayette, Louisiana.

1645
01:15:00.010 --> 01:15:03.290
I was born.

1646
01:15:03.870 --> 01:15:04.390
Lafayette.

1647
01:15:04.510 --> 01:15:05.050
And you know what?

1648
01:15:05.150 --> 01:15:07.530
I love the slogan for their shoe store.

1649
01:15:07.530 --> 01:15:10.470
If you go on their website, it's a clothing boutique and shoes.

1650
01:15:10.670 --> 01:15:14.890
But their slogan is, life is short, buy the damn shoes.

1651
01:15:16.710 --> 01:15:17.990
That is amazing.

1652
01:15:18.310 --> 01:15:22.950
So there are two Shulalas, Michael, but none of them seem to sell men's shoes.

1653
01:15:22.950 --> 01:15:27.890
Oh, well, I would love nothing more for Michael to have Shulala.

1654
01:15:28.930 --> 01:15:32.530
Well, we have a great reverse talking head.

1655
01:15:32.790 --> 01:15:33.870
Yes, I noticed.

1656
01:15:34.330 --> 01:15:39.330
So Dwight is in Michael's chair and you pull back to reveal Michael perched behind him.

1657
01:15:39.710 --> 01:15:43.050
Basically, in this talking head, Michael's like, he's going to do it for me.

1658
01:15:43.170 --> 01:15:43.750
He's going to do it.

1659
01:15:43.850 --> 01:15:44.830
He's going to take the fall.

1660
01:15:45.090 --> 01:15:46.650
And Dwight's like, no, I haven't decided.

1661
01:15:47.210 --> 01:15:49.610
Well, folks in the office are starting to catch on.

1662
01:15:49.750 --> 01:15:50.550
They get it.

1663
01:15:50.690 --> 01:15:51.730
They know what Michael's doing.

1664
01:15:51.730 --> 01:15:56.930
He wants Dwight to take the fall and they start gossiping about it.

1665
01:15:57.290 --> 01:16:05.230
There's a scene in the kitchen, you guys, that was deleted where Meredith, Kelly and Angela and Oscar are all being real chatty.

1666
01:16:05.450 --> 01:16:10.670
And Michael walks in and overhears a bit and he's spying on them from the bathroom.

1667
01:16:10.970 --> 01:16:11.530
Let's hear it.

1668
01:16:11.910 --> 01:16:12.390
Ladies.

1669
01:16:13.630 --> 01:16:14.110
Really?

1670
01:16:14.850 --> 01:16:15.330
It's...

1671
01:16:15.330 --> 01:16:18.050
I hope Dwight gets fired and we get a hot new guy to replace them.

1672
01:16:18.290 --> 01:16:18.570
Seriously?

1673
01:16:18.930 --> 01:16:19.830
What if it's a hot new girl?

1674
01:16:20.250 --> 01:16:21.530
Oh my God, I had not thought of that.

1675
01:16:22.030 --> 01:16:23.950
I think it's horrible what Michael is doing.

1676
01:16:24.690 --> 01:16:25.070
Really.

1677
01:16:25.390 --> 01:16:26.630
I mean, this is unacceptable.

1678
01:16:32.740 --> 01:16:36.300
Hey, did you ever notice that our bathroom is right next to our kitchen?

1679
01:16:37.460 --> 01:16:38.560
How's that up to code?

1680
01:16:40.610 --> 01:16:41.370
I don't know.

1681
01:16:44.830 --> 01:16:46.950
This is not fair what he's doing to Dwight.

1682
01:16:47.050 --> 01:16:47.870
Of course you think that.

1683
01:16:47.950 --> 01:16:48.650
You used to bone my guy.

1684
01:16:49.130 --> 01:16:50.290
I think men bone women.

1685
01:16:50.510 --> 01:16:51.530
I hate that I'm correcting that.

1686
01:16:51.530 --> 01:16:54.570
All I'm saying is, is that Dwight can't take the blame for this.

1687
01:16:54.790 --> 01:16:55.950
It has to land on Michael.

1688
01:16:56.350 --> 01:16:57.610
It's time for a reckoning.

1689
01:16:57.790 --> 01:16:57.990
It's true.

1690
01:16:59.130 --> 01:16:59.530
Okay.

1691
01:16:59.530 --> 01:17:02.850
Hey, these are the kind of slice of life.

1692
01:17:03.450 --> 01:17:04.370
Slice-o-life.

1693
01:17:04.610 --> 01:17:05.350
Slice-o-life.

1694
01:17:05.450 --> 01:17:06.150
You brought it back.

1695
01:17:06.370 --> 01:17:11.470
These are the kind of slice-o-life office moments that I love so much.

1696
01:17:11.470 --> 01:17:12.790
Just the scuttlebutt.

1697
01:17:12.810 --> 01:17:14.390
There's so much going on.

1698
01:17:14.530 --> 01:17:16.730
Just the gossip and the opinions.

1699
01:17:16.910 --> 01:17:17.210
Uh-huh.

1700
01:17:17.350 --> 01:17:17.990
You know?

1701
01:17:17.990 --> 01:17:19.550
I loved this scene.

1702
01:17:19.830 --> 01:17:21.930
And Michael overhears it, you guys.

1703
01:17:22.070 --> 01:17:25.810
And there's a whole scene where Michael confronts everyone.

1704
01:17:26.330 --> 01:17:28.830
And he really lets them have it.

1705
01:17:28.930 --> 01:17:30.990
He goes barging into the bullpen.

1706
01:17:30.990 --> 01:17:32.490
And he's like, hey, everyone.

1707
01:17:32.510 --> 01:17:34.130
I need to make an announcement.

1708
01:17:34.150 --> 01:17:36.110
And Jim is like, this is a new record.

1709
01:17:36.350 --> 01:17:40.790
And Michael goes, that's because I have a lot to say today, James.

1710
01:17:41.650 --> 01:17:42.250
Uh-huh.

1711
01:17:42.350 --> 01:17:43.390
He's ticked off.

1712
01:17:43.510 --> 01:17:45.170
And then he goes around the room.

1713
01:17:45.270 --> 01:17:47.070
And he's like, yells to the room,

1714
01:17:47.070 --> 01:17:49.570
have you wondered what it would be like if I was fired?

1715
01:17:49.810 --> 01:17:52.230
And everyone, super happy, raises their hand.

1716
01:17:52.530 --> 01:17:54.650
And Michael's like, damn it.

1717
01:17:54.790 --> 01:17:56.910
I didn't ask for a show of hands.

1718
01:17:57.230 --> 01:18:00.070
If I get fired and corporate brings in new leadership,

1719
01:18:00.070 --> 01:18:02.030
you have no idea who might come.

1720
01:18:02.190 --> 01:18:04.690
And then he starts singling people out.

1721
01:18:04.950 --> 01:18:08.490
He says, you have no idea how bad it could get.

1722
01:18:08.670 --> 01:18:13.090
Maybe it would be someone who knows that we don't actually need three accountants.

1723
01:18:13.470 --> 01:18:15.410
I remember shooting this scene now.

1724
01:18:15.490 --> 01:18:15.970
Yes.

1725
01:18:15.970 --> 01:18:17.670
It's in the deleted scenes.

1726
01:18:17.870 --> 01:18:19.610
Then he looks right at Jim and Pam.

1727
01:18:19.690 --> 01:18:24.670
And he says, or let's couples work together without sending them to different branches.

1728
01:18:25.610 --> 01:18:28.270
And then he has this moment and made me laugh.

1729
01:18:28.350 --> 01:18:31.450
He goes, so you didn't think about that, huh?

1730
01:18:31.650 --> 01:18:35.630
So let's just bite our tongues instead of saying mean things about me

1731
01:18:35.630 --> 01:18:38.630
when I pretend to be pooping in the bathroom, OK?

1732
01:18:40.660 --> 01:18:42.080
But it was a long speech.

1733
01:18:42.080 --> 01:18:43.980
And he really just lets them all have it.

1734
01:18:44.180 --> 01:18:45.900
I love this episode so much.

1735
01:18:45.900 --> 01:18:50.340
I think Steve Carell just is brilliant in this episode.

1736
01:18:50.420 --> 01:18:52.460
He's playing so many different things.

1737
01:18:52.740 --> 01:18:57.080
We already talked about this with Rain, but I just absolutely love the Michael Dwight dynamic.

1738
01:18:57.640 --> 01:18:59.320
I really loved this one.

1739
01:18:59.540 --> 01:19:00.180
I did too.

1740
01:19:00.360 --> 01:19:03.040
This was like one of those sleeper ones that we hadn't seen in forever.

1741
01:19:03.200 --> 01:19:04.620
And we're like, oh my gosh, golden ticket.

1742
01:19:04.840 --> 01:19:05.380
I agree.

1743
01:19:05.740 --> 01:19:07.140
Golden ticket is a golden ticket.

1744
01:19:07.480 --> 01:19:09.480
Well, now David Wallace is going to show up.

1745
01:19:09.560 --> 01:19:11.200
He drove from New York, you guys.

1746
01:19:12.100 --> 01:19:15.280
David Wallace arrives at the office, right?

1747
01:19:15.460 --> 01:19:17.300
This is a serious thing.

1748
01:19:17.660 --> 01:19:17.840
Yeah.

1749
01:19:18.340 --> 01:19:20.200
